BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:TDPS presents “Orestes: An Antic Tragedy” transadapted by Anne
  Washburn from the play by Euripides — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261122T000000
DTSTAMP:20261123T235726Z
UID:0b65fdaa329a97c256ba9fd8d12d@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Performing Arts\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United
  States
DESCRIPTION:Transadapted by Anne Washburn from the play by Euripides Direc
 ted by Susannah Martin “The Trojan war is over. Orestes and Electra have
  killed their mother. The city wants them dead. Just when it seems like th
 ey have nowhere to turn\, their best friend comes up with a plan… Ironic
 \, desperate\, humorous\, and highly entertaining\, this potent satire on 
 the Oresteia myth brings this marvelous play to new life.” This transada
 ptation by Anne Washburn brings Euripides’ Orestes into the 21st century
 . Euripides wrote from a place of experimentation and innovation\, infusin
 g the classic tragedy with irony\, skepticism toward the gods\, and a vehe
 ment anti-war stance. Just as urgent today as it was then\, Ore\nCategory:
  Performing Arts\nOriginal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/TDPS/event
 /322099-tdps-presents-orestes-an-antic-tragedy-transadapted-b
LOCATION:Zellerbach Playhouse\, Zellerbach Playhouse
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/TDPS/event/322099-tdps-presents-orestes-an
 -antic-tragedy-transadapted-b
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
