BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Rouge — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261122T180000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261122T190000
DTSTAMP:20261123T235726Z
UID:c14861f3740d54640bd934aca902@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Rouge is a sensuous and melancholy film about a beautiful ghos
 t searching for her lost lover in modern Hong Kong. Fleur (Anita Mui) and 
 “Twelfth Master” (Leslie Cheung) committed suicide fifty years ago\, i
 ntending to spend eternity together in Hell rather than be separated by hi
 s disapproving parents. But when “Twelfth Master” fails to join her in
  the afterlife\, Fleur returns to Earth to find him. She befriends a journ
 alist couple. Fascinated by her archaic clothes\, language\, and otherworl
 dly manner\, they agree to help. Slipping back and forth in time\, “ Rou
 ge is something like the Platonic ideal of a cinematic ghost story” (Den
 nis Lim\, Criterion Collection).\nCategory: Films\nOriginal listing: https
 ://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331162-film-screening-rouge
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CANCELLED
URL:https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331162-film-screening-rouge
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:berkeley-arts
END:VEVENT
