SUMMARY:The Doctrine Film Screening – First Voices Festival — Atlanta
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261127T190000
DTEND;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261127T210000
DTSTAMP:20261123T235726Z
UID:771dd2801dfbb23e005034d31bff@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Film + TV\,Atlanta\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Special screening of Gwendolen Cates’s film The Doctrine for
  First Voices Festival This film follows a group of Indigenous teenagers f
 rom Minneapolis/St. Paul who travel to Rome to meet with Vatican officials
  and advocate for the repudiation of the Doctrine. Also featured are Indig
 enous activists in Aotearoa New Zealand\, Guatemala\, New Caledonia\, and 
 Puerto Rico. The film exposes how the Doctrine of Discovery has targeted c
 ommunities of color\, was the origin of the transatlantic slave trade\, an
 d enables corporate forces driving the climate crisis. “The Doctrine of 
 Discovery” is the term for 15th-century decrees issued by the Vatican th
 at authorized conquest and colonization\, codified racism \nCategory: Film
  + TV\nOriginal listing: https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-doctrine-film-s
 creening-first-voices-festival/
LOCATION:Plaza Theatre\, 1049 Ponce De Leon Ave. NE\, Atlanta\, GA\, 30306
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://www.artsatl.org/event/the-doctrine-film-screening-first-voices
 -festival/
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-REGION:us
X-GLOBAL-CULTURE-SOURCE:artsatl
END:VEVENT
