DESCRIPTION:In the introduction to this digital publication\, written by I
 nés Plasencia Camps\, we read: “Bodies ‘feel’ fear—though not the
  same fear—when they cross paths. They cannot shed their history\; it is
  from within that history that they inevitably experience fear.” Four ye
 ars after our programmes exploring fear and artistic practices\, The Names
  of Fear (2021) and Fear\, Love and Revolution (2022)—which examined thi
 s emotion as a central axis of contemporary social relations—we present 
 a publication gathering part of what took place then\, alongside essays wr
 itten especially for this book\, born out of a desire to keep the conversa
 tion going. Guided by the urgency of continuing to talk about fear\, th\nC
 ategory: Multidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.o
 rg/en/schedule/book-launch-names-fear-fear-love-and-revolution
