UID:99fedef329e59c703f7233991c9a@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:For Freedoms presents artist and educator Eric Gottesman’s N
 IGHT AND DAY which centers on Ethiopian journalist and author Baalu Girma
 ’s controversial 1984 Amharic novel Oromay\, written under the Derg regi
 me and banned shortly after its publication. Drawing on Gottesman’s deep
  engagement with the novel\, NIGHT AND DAY considers how artists create\, 
 communicate\, and sustain cultural memory within and against conditions of
  censorship\, political repression\, and state violence. The exhibition ex
 tends beyond the gallery through a library of banned books\, a self-guided
  workshop station that invites visitors to respond to censorship through w
 riting and drawing\, and a public conversation on how artists\nCategory: A
 rts & Culture\nOriginal listing: https://calendar.gwu.edu/event/eric-gotte
 smans-night-and-day
LOCATION:Flagg Building\, 500 17th Street NW\, Washington DC 20006
